# Environment variable template for this project.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` (and every `.env*` except this example) is gitignored, so
# real secrets never reach version control. Supply only non-sensitive
# placeholders here. See the Security & Secrets guide for the full policy:
# https://github.com/tannergolden/standards/blob/Development/docs/operations/Security-&-Secrets.md
#
# Replace the samples below with the variables your project actually needs.

# This repository's commands read these from the shell or from make's command
# line, such as `make test BUILD_FLAGS=...`; none of them is a secret.

# The image `make build` tags and `make test-image` checks.
# IMAGE=environment:local
# Extra flags for docker build, such as a CA bundle behind a proxy that
# inspects TLS: --secret id=ca-bundle,src=/path/to/ca-bundle.crt
# BUILD_FLAGS=
# The release `make cloud-setup` pins the cloud setup script to.
# VERSION=v1.0.0
# The image the tests in tests/image/ check, which make test-image sets.
# ENVIRONMENT_IMAGE=environment:local
# Where toolchain/install.sh fetches its archives from instead of the public
# hosts; the pins still decide what is installed.
# ENVIRONMENT_MIRROR=
